    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0394" n="386" xml:id="pg386"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20291/16</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Assistant Chief of
                        the Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Alling</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-29">July 29, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <table>
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell rendition="#nowrap #top">Participants:</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Nevile Butler, Minister-Counselor of
                            British Embassy.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Murray<anchor n="63" xml:id="d363-f1"
                            /></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Alling</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>Mr. Butler said that a few days ago Mr. Maisky, the Soviet Ambassador at London,
                    suggested to Mr. Eden<anchor n="64" xml:id="d363-f2"/> that the British and
                    Soviet Governments make joint representations to the Iranian Government urging
                    it to get rid of between 5,000 and 10,000 German agents operating in Iran. Mr.
                    Butler said that Mr. Eden had agreed to this proposal and that the joint
                    representations had been made in Tehran a day or two ago. He said that the
                    Iranian reply was noncommittal.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d363-f1" n="63" xml:id="d363-f1-content">
                <p>Wallace Murray, Chief of the Division of Near Eastern Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d363-f2" n="64" xml:id="d363-f2-content">
                <p>Anthony Eden, British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
